<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomPermission xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-31, wire-fraud prerequisite gate, THIRD code-review pass). Story 28
        added Prerequisite_Must_Be_Met_To_Complete (validation rule, SYSTEM_MODE backstop) plus
        TaskPrerequisiteService's before-update trigger gate, which refuses ANY change to a checklist
        item's identity fields (Blocked_By__c, and by extension the Transaction_Deal__c / Task_Group__c
        / Task_Sequence__c fields a repointed key depends on) on an OPEN row that would defeat the
        gate - for EVERY principal and EVERY write path, INCLUDING AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE, because it
        is a before-update trigger with no bypass switch. That refusal is correct for the fraud case it
        exists to stop, but it also blocks three legitimate operations that need to touch those same
        fields: (1) scripts/backfill-task-blocked-by.apex, which runs as ANONYMOUS APEX and therefore
        enforces the running user's own FLS - it cannot use AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE at all (unavailable
        in anonymous Apex); (2) the M5 migration's mass key-clear, the documented retirement path for
        this whole Phase-0 control once Checklist_Item__c replaces Task; and (3) Phase 1's
        Blocked_By_Sequence__c renumbering and the repair of a mis-fanned deal whose key is wrong but
        still resolvable to a real (incorrect) row - neither repairable nor completable by anyone today
        without this permission, because "wrong but resolvable" is not the same as "unresolvable and
        therefore already exempt" (a wrong key can name a real row, and TaskPrerequisiteService's
        refusal fires exactly the same for that case as for a fraud attempt).

        This custom permission is the legitimate route TaskPrerequisiteService checks (via
        FeatureManagement.checkPermission) before allowing an identity-field change on an open row that
        its default rule would otherwise refuse. It does NOT weaken Prerequisite_Must_Be_Met_To_Complete
        itself (the SYSTEM_MODE validation-rule backstop on Status = 'Completed' is unconditional and
        this permission has no bearing on it) - it only widens who may edit the KEY fields the gate
        reads, and is deliberately narrow and admin-only, never granted to the working Transaction team.

        🔴 THE API NAME IS PINNED — Transaction_Prereq_Override — TaskPrerequisiteService is being wired
        to this exact name via FeatureManagement.checkPermission('Transaction_Prereq_Override') in the
        same review pass. Do not rename.

        SHAPE MATCHES Transaction_Task_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml and
        Transaction_Stage_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml (read both before touching this file):
        object-level/gate-level CRUD that cannot be granted any other way on this platform, authorized
        by a named custom permission read via FeatureManagement.checkPermission, with the FLS/DML grant
        living on a dedicated permission set - here, Transaction_Prereq_Override_Access, an ADMIN-ONLY
        set, deliberately NOT a member of DPEG_Transaction_Team and NOT added to DPEG_Admin_Access (that
        file was mid-edit by a concurrent session on a Disposition tranche at the time this was
        written; a PermissionSet deploy REPLACES its whole fieldPermissions set, so touching it here
        would risk shipping or clobbering that unrelated work - see
        Transaction_Prereq_Override_Access.permissionset-meta.xml for the full reasoning).

        SCOPE IS THE FOUR WIRE-FRAUD-GATE IDENTITY FIELDS ONLY (Blocked_By__c, Transaction_Deal__c,
        Task_Group__c, Task_Sequence__c on Task/Event). It does not authorize Task completion itself -
        that remains Transaction_Task_Actions' job - and it does not cover Disposition, which has no
        equivalent gate today.
    -->
    <label>Transaction Prereq Override</label>
    <description>Authorization letting an admin-only path repoint the wire-fraud prerequisite gate's identity fields (Blocked_By__c and the fields a key depends on) on an open checklist item, for the backfill script, the M5 migration and Phase 1 key repair.</description>
    <isLicensed>false</isLicensed>
</CustomPermission>
